# ControlRig Solver Intent Validation Design

Date: 2026-06-30

Status: validation-only, no sample/live proof captured.

This note records the sampleless Phase 7A step for solver work. It does not
approve solver unit expansion. It lets MCP callers describe intended solver
families and receive read-only evidence that the plan is shaped correctly
before any ControlRig asset, RigVM graph, or AnimBP is built.

## Boundary

- `validate_controlrig_solver_intents` is an UnrealMCP-owned native preflight;
  the Python FastMCP wrapper only dispatches the request to the bridge.
- `validation_only_no_sample` is the only accepted gate status.
- `build_allowed=false`.
- `asset_mutation_allowed=false`.
- `requires_sample_live_proof=true`.
- no sample/temp live proof was captured in this pass.
- no ControlRig authoring module entry point, C++ solver allowlist, recipe
  writer, RigVM node creation, compile, save, or direct solve proof is added by
  this design.
- no static dependency from `UnrealMCP` to `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`.
- no MCP-only reference is serialized into any generated asset, because this
  pass generates no asset.

## First Validation Candidate

The current sampleless candidate is a two-bone IK limb intent:

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| intent kind | `two_bone_ik_limb` |
| candidate unit | `FRigUnit_TwoBoneIKSimplePerItem` |
| Unreal display family | `Basic IK` |
| required bones | `root_bone`, `mid_bone`, `end_bone` |
| required controls | `target_control`, `pole_control` |
| required curve | `weight_curve` |

This candidate is deliberately not a C++ allowlist entry yet. The validator
accepts only the intent metadata and rejects materialized `rigvm.units` entries
for `FRigUnit_TwoBoneIKSimplePerItem` or other pose-changing solver units.

## Accepted Request Shape

```json
{
  "target_control_rig_path": "/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype",
  "solver_gate": {
    "status": "validation_only_no_sample",
    "allows_build": false,
    "allows_asset_mutation": false,
    "requires_sample_live_proof": true
  },
  "solver_intents": [
    {
      "kind": "two_bone_ik_limb",
      "name": "LeftArm",
      "side": "left",
      "candidate_unit_struct": "FRigUnit_TwoBoneIKSimplePerItem",
      "root_bone": "upperarm_l",
      "mid_bone": "lowerarm_l",
      "end_bone": "hand_l",
      "target_control": "PiperStable_LeftArm_Target",
      "pole_control": "PiperStable_LeftArm_Pole",
      "weight_curve": "PiperStable_LeftArm_Weight"
    }
  ]
}
```

`compile_controlrig_profile_recipe` can emit the same validation-only intent
metadata when called with `include_solver_intents=true`. That compiler output
still reports `adds_solver_units=false` and must not be passed to a solver
writer, because no solver writer exists in this phase.

## Validation Rules

The validator fails when:

- `solver_gate` is missing or not exactly `validation_only_no_sample`;
- `allows_build`, `allows_asset_mutation`, or save/build/execute flags are
  enabled;
- `target_control_rig_path` is outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp` or
  `/Game/_MCP_Sample`;
- `solver_intents` is empty;
- an intent has an unknown `kind`, invalid `side`, unstable name, duplicate
  name, missing required field, or repeated root/mid/end bone;
- a provided hierarchy spec is missing the named control, curve, or bone;
- `rigvm.units` already contains a pose-changing solver unit such as
  `FRigUnit_TwoBoneIKSimplePerItem`, `FRigUnit_SetTransform`, or FABRIK/Aim/
  spline variants.

## Phase 2 Hand-Off

The next solver implementation can start only after a sample/temp live proof
is available and a reviewed task explicitly approves solver unit expansion.
That future task must add a narrow C++ allowlist entry, recipe schema,
pin-default validation, compile/readback checks, direct solve proof, and cleanup
evidence. Until then this design is evidence only.
